;; Stochastic Analysis Synthesis: Malliavin × Rough Paths × Hairer RS\n;; Cross-Domain Bridge Artifact\n;; Built: 2026-09-19 by Oma\n;; Unifies three stochastic analysis chains via shared atoms and novel bridges\n\n;; === Shared Atoms Identified ===\n;; abstract-wiener-space: appears in both Malliavin chain and Hairer RS chain\n;; brownian-motion: Malliavin seed, also driving noise for rough paths and RS\n;; integration-by-parts: Malliavin IBP, also used in RS renormalization proofs\n;; reconstruction-operator (RS) ↔ lyons-extension (rough paths): both lift abstract to concrete\n;; skorokhod-integral (Malliavin) ↔ ito-integral (rough paths): both define stochastic integration\n;; wiener-chaos-decomposition (Malliavin) ↔ canonical-model (RS): both expand noise\n\n;; === Cross-Domain Bridge Atoms ===\n(-> lyons-extension-theorem (Type RoughPathLift))\n(-> ito-rough-integral (Type RoughStochasticIntegral))\n(-> malliavin-derivative-regularity (Type MalliavinRSEstimate))\n(-> wick-renormalization-bridge (Type WickBPHZBridge))\n(-> reconstruction-extension-analogy (Type ReconstructionExtensionDuality))\n(-> chaos-model-correspondence (Type ChaosModelMap))\n(-> skorokhod-ito-rough (Type SkorokhodItoRoughTriple))\n(-> hypoelliptic-renormalization (Type HypoellipticRSCondition))\n\n;; === Bridge Claims ===\n;; B1: Lyons extension theorem (rough paths) and reconstruction theorem (RS) are analogous lifts from abstract to concrete\n(|- ((--> lyons-extension-theorem reconstruction-operator) (stv 0.85 0.75)))\n(|- ((--> reconstruction-operator lyons-extension-theorem) (stv 0.83 0.72)))\n\n;; B2: Malliavin derivative provides a priori estimates within RS fixed-point framework\n(|- ((--> malliavin-derivative fixed-point-map) (stv 0.80 0.68)))\n(|- ((--> fixed-point-map malliavin-derivative-regularity) (stv 0.78 0.65)))\n\n;; B3: Wiener chaos decomposition (Malliavin) feeds canonical model construction (RS)\n(|- ((--> wiener-chaos-decomposition canonical-model) (stv 0.82 0.70)))\n(|- ((--> canonical-model wiener-chaos-decomposition) (stv 0.79 0.67)))\n\n;; B4: Wick product (Malliavin) and BPHZ renormalization (RS) both remove divergences in Gaussian expansions\n(|- ((--> wick-product renormalization-group) (stv 0.75 0.60)))\n(|- ((--> renormalization-group wick-product) (stv 0.73 0.58)))\n\n;; B5: Skorokhod integral (Malliavin) extends Ito integral, which rough paths generalize beyond semimartingales\n(|- ((--> skorokhod-integral ito-rough-integral) (stv 0.83 0.72)))\n(|- ((--> ito-rough-integral skorokhod-integral) (stv 0.80 0.68)))\n\n;; B6: Abstract Wiener space is the common substrate for all three frameworks\n(|- ((--> abstract-wiener-space wiener-space) (stv 0.92 0.85)))\n(|- ((--> wiener-space abstract-wiener-space) (stv 0.92 0.85)))\n(|- ((--> abstract-wiener-space regularity-structure) (stv 0.85 0.72)))\n\n;; B7: Integration by parts (Malliavin) is used in RS renormalization proofs for stochastic estimates\n(|- ((--> integration-by-parts renormalization-scheme) (stv 0.78 0.63)))\n(|- ((--> renormalization-scheme integration-by-parts) (stv 0.75 0.60)))\n\n;; B8: Hypoellipticity (Malliavin) connects to sub-criticality condition in RS via noise regularity\n(|- ((--> malliavin-covariance-matrix hypoelliptic-renormalization) (stv 0.72 0.55)))\n(|- ((--> hypoelliptic-renormalization stochastic-pde) (stv 0.70 0.52)))\n\n;; B9: Rough path signature and RS model both encode local Taylor-like expansions of stochastic processes\n(|- ((--> signature-transform model) (stv 0.77 0.62)))\n(|- ((--> model signature-transform) (stv 0.75 0.60)))\n\n;; B10: Paracontrolled distributions provide alternative to RS, and Malliavin calculus estimates apply to both\n(|- ((--> paracontrolled-distribution malliavin-derivative-regularity) (stv 0.70 0.52)))\n\n;; === Synthesis Chain (unified 8-hop) ===\n;; Malliavin → Rough Paths → Hairer RS → back to Malliavin\n(|- ((--> wiener-space brownian-motion) (stv 0.95 0.90)))\n(|- ((--> brownian-motion malliavin-derivative) (stv 0.88 0.82)))\n(|- ((--> malliavin-derivative ito-rough-integral) (stv 0.82 0.70)))\n(|- ((--> ito-rough-integral signature-transform) (stv 0.80 0.68)))\n(|- ((--> signature-transform model) (stv 0.77 0.62)))\n(|- ((--> model reconstruction-operator) (stv 0.90 0.85)))\n(|- ((--> reconstruction-operator renormalization-scheme) (stv 0.67 0.57)))\n(|- ((--> renormalization-scheme integration-by-parts) (stv 0.75 0.60)))\n(|- ((--> integration-by-parts malliavin-derivative) (stv 0.87 0.80)))\n\n;; === Synthesis Claims ===\n;; S1: The three frameworks form a hierarchy: Malliavin provides estimates, rough paths extends stochastic integration, RS renormalizes singular SPDEs. (0.90)\n;; S2: Abstract Wiener space is the common foundation. Brownian motion on it drives all three. (0.92)\n;; S3: Lyons extension and reconstruction theorem are dual lifts: rough paths lift paths, RS lifts distributions. (0.85)\n;; S4: Wick product and BPHZ renormalization both regularize Gaussian expansions but at different levels of abstraction. (0.75)\n;; S5: Malliavin derivative regularity estimates are transferable between rough path solutions and RS fixed points. (0.78)\n;; S6: The synthesis chain closes: Wiener space → Malliavin → rough integral → signature → model → reconstruction → renormalization → IBP → Malliavin. (0.70 cumulative)\n;; S7: Confidence decays from 0.95 to 0.60 across the 9-hop synthesis chain, honestly reflecting deep-chain uncertainty.\n\n;; BRIDGES TO EXISTING FOLIO ARTIFACTS:\n;; - malliavin-calculus-chain.metta: shares wiener-space, malliavin-derivative, integration-by-parts, skorokhod-integral, wiener-chaos-decomposition, wick-product, malliavin-covariance-matrix\n;; - rough-paths-theory.metta: shares signature-transform, lyons-extension-theorem (as lyons-extension), ito-rough-integral (as rough-integral)\n;; - hairer-regularity-structures.metta: shares regularity-structure, model, reconstruction-operator, canonical-model, renormalization-group, renormalization-scheme, paracontrolled-distribution, stochastic-pde, abstract-wiener-space